# {title}

{description}

Made with `modelly new --template plugin`. The package `{package}/` holds a design sampler;
`pyproject.toml` declares it under the `modelly.samplers` entry-point group and says which
Modelly versions it supports (`{requirement}`).

## Set up and test

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate            # Windows: .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python -m pip install -e ".[dev]"
python -m pytest
modelly plugins --check              # the sampler is found, compatible and loads
```

## Use it

```toml
# an experiment file (modelly experiment run study.toml)
[design]
kind = "{package}_jitter"
n = 20
```

Add a space, an executor, a collector, a Studio view or a lint rule the same way: one module,
one entry point in its group. The groups and what each entry point must name are in the
[plugins guide](https://remipelloux.github.io/Modelly/dev/plugins.html).
